+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders, especially a switch to email to save money. Reminders go
+by SMS because the April–June 2025 email trial was followed by more missed pickups and wasted fresh food.
+
+## Sending reminders
+
+[The reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) sends a member their pickup slot the day before pickup.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+SMS reminders cost €40 a month. Email offered a way to remove that cost, so the pantry tried email reminders from
+April to June 2025. According to the provider's report cited in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), 34% of reminder
+emails were never opened. Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag,
+and its fresh food went in the bin at closing time.
+
+The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone in the family and never check email, but do see SMS.
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025; by August, missed pickups were back to 6%.
+
+The maintainer confirmed keeping SMS in issue 52 after another proposal to save its cost. The monthly SMS expense
+is accepted because the email trial's savings came with more missed pickups and food waste. A future proposal to
+change channels needs to address whether members will see the reminders and collect their pantry orders, as well
+as the sending cost.
